[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IDD001
TITLE: Concrete schemas for IRS001 through IRS004
STATEMENT: >>>
The design shall represent a pilot clearance as a map with aircraft, runway, sequence, kind, wind, and text fields. A neighbor message shall be a tuple of request, accept, reject, or stale with the aircraft identity. The TOML schema shall match IRS003. A log command shall be a tuple of the clearance kind and its arguments. Acceptance is a round trip that encodes one landing clearance and one handoff accept and decodes them to the same fields.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The interface requirements need one concrete representation so tests can construct messages.
<<<
DAL: A
REQUIREMENT_LEVEL: Low-Level
VERIFICATION: Test
ASSUMPTIONS: Erlang maps and tuples are the concrete syntax. They are not a wire standard beyond this CSCI.
